#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid "Templates for Grimoire"
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid ""
"Copy pictures here to write on them as paper: PNG or JPG files, upright, in "
"the shape of a Kindle Scribe page (3:4). 1860 x 2480 pixels is best. Light "
"lines on white work best on e-ink: dark areas hide your writing."
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid ""
"Copy them in over USB while Grimoire is closed. A notebook keeps its own "
"copy of each template it uses, so changing or deleting a file here never "
"changes pages already written on it. Grimoire keeps its previews of these "
"files in the .cache folder."
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid "Photos for Grimoire"
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid ""
"Copy photos here to write on them: JPG or PNG files, as your phone or camera "
"saved them. In a notebook, open Paper and pick Photos...: the photo becomes "
"the open page's paper, fitted to the page and turned upright. For a page of "
"its own, add a new page in Pages first."
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid ""
"Copy them in over USB while Grimoire is closed. A notebook keeps its own "
"copy of each photo it uses, so changing or deleting a file here never "
"changes pages already written on it. Grimoire keeps its previews of these "
"files in the .cache folder."
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid "Importing pages into Grimoire"
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid ""
"To write on pages you already have, such as a PDF saved as pictures, put a "
"folder of PNG or JPG files here, one picture a page, and start Grimoire. The "
"folder's name becomes the notebook's name, and the pages follow the file "
"names in order (page-2 comes before page-10). Gray pictures import faster "
"and take less room than colour ones."
msgstr ""

#: rust/src/bgwork_template.rs
msgid ""
"Grimoire imports each folder in the background and then moves it into the "
"done folder. Copy folders in over USB while Grimoire is closed."
msgstr ""

